            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why does the shown strict equality check display its result?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"906\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" === \" /><text value=\"9006\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"false\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It displays <code>false</code> because <code>906</code> and <code>9006</code> are different numbers</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It displays <code>true</code> because both values are numbers</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">It displays <code>9069006</code> because <code>===</code> joins numbers</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It displays <code>false</code> because <code>906</code> and <code>9006</code> are different numbers.</p></body></html>"
